  "body": "Stacked on #1131 (→ #560 → #551). Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n- **Sinker Burn passes** (sibling ops, one electrode per op): each Sinker Burn gains `pass` (single / rough / finish; single keeps #541's law unchanged) and the finished cavity `cavity_x` / `cavity_y`.\n- **Undersize law** (`motion::sinker_undersize::judge`): a rough or finish reads its condition's `undersize` and `gap` through #531's `Edm::condition` by id, after the sinker-kind check (`sinker_op::condition`, the door the gap and undersize now share). Per axis it refuses by name: electrode + 2×gap wider than the cavity (the wall would be burned past size), a finish that burns short of the cavity (\"sinker finish leaves the cavity under size\"), and an electrode that is not `cavity - 2×undersize`. The tip stands one undersize above the finished floor (`SinkerParams.stand`), so a rough leaves `undersize - gap` on floor and walls alike.\n- **Order law**: a finish looks back (program order, same setup, unsuppressed) for the rough of the same cavity. If its undersize is not smaller, a new advisory `Warning::SinkerFinishOrder` names both numbers. It does not hold the post, because the finish's own size law already holds the cavity to size.\n- Stamp digests the undersize and the rough a finish follows. DTO keys are additive and written only for rough or finish. The UI Passes tab gains the pass and the cavity X/Y.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/543-sinker-undersize.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- `sinker_undersize.rs` (new):\n  - `a_rough_finish_pair_reaches_the_finished_size_in_the_sim`: the program verdict with the box atom. After the rough, stock stands and nothing is gouged. After the finish, `dev.is_clean()`. Writes golden `sinker_rough_finish_pair.cl`.\n  - `a_finish_that_leaves_the_cavity_under_size_is_refused_by_name`: under size, wrong electrode, overburn, no undersize and no cavity are each refused.\n  - `a_finish_no_smaller_in_undersize_than_its_rough_is_warned_by_name`\n  - `a_rough_finish_pair_round_trips_the_file`\n  - `the_rough_finish_pair_is_driven_over_mcp_with_the_gui_commands`: add_operation, edit_operation, generate and undo. No new MCP tool is needed.\n- `motion::sinker_undersize::tests::sinker_undersize_judges_rough_and_finish` (unit).\n- Quick gate, run locally: sim lib, motion lib, app lib plus sinker_burn, sinker_undersize, mcp, warned_moves, verify, project_roundtrip, operations, edm_conditions, edm_machine, stock_stamp, commands_undo, ribbon and tool_law. Also ui lib and ui operations. All green. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- Not exercised on a real EDM control: the conditions are synthetic. The full app suite that `xtask gate quick` selects (because a golden was added) was not run; the touched suites listed above were. Orbiting finishes (#544) and the post (#542) are out of scope.\n\nChangelog: Sinker EDM rough and finish burns: per-side undersize from the machine's conditions, an under-size finish refused, an inverted pair warned (#543)\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #543\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
